---
title: Governance wrapper order
---
%% Source of truth: packages/harness/src/felix/manifests/builder.py, the block
%% commented "Governance pipeline (order matters)". Each apply_* clones the tool
%% with a new executor, so registration order IS call-path nesting: the LAST one
%% applied runs FIRST on the way in, and LAST on the way out.
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What a tool call passes through, inbound and outbound
    accDescr: A model's tool call enters at the outermost wrapper and unwinds back out through the same stack. Artifact spill is outermost, so it sees the final content; secret masking is innermost, so it redacts before any other wrapper reads output. Approvals can suspend the call and wait for a human decision, and policies, command screening, content screening, limits and guardrails can each deny it outright — a denial short-circuits the rest of the stack and returns a deny_output to the model. Command screening can also require approval rather than deny outright, so a run can be suspended from two places in the stack. Only controls the manifest enables are installed, with one exception: limits is always applied, because gating it on any_limit() once left manifests with no tool-call cap, no wall clock, and no spend ceiling.

    subgraph stack["Governance stack — outermost to innermost"]
        direction TB
        spill["apply_artifact_spill<br/>spec.artifacts"] -->|"pauses run, writes approvals row"| appr["apply_approvals<br/>spec.approvals"]
        appr --> judges["apply_judges<br/>spec.guardrails.judges"]
        judges --> guard["apply_guardrails<br/>spec.guardrails"]
        guard -->|"tool-call count, wall clock, tokens, spend"| limits["apply_limits<br/>always installed"]
        limits --> content["apply_content_screening<br/>PII + injection"]
        content -->|"command text of sandbox and container tools"| command["apply_command_screening"]
        command -->|"first matching rule wins"| policies["apply_policies<br/>spec.policies"]
        policies --> mask["apply_secret_masking<br/>innermost"]
    end

    mask -->|"runs the real executor"| exec(["Bound tool executor"])
    exec -.->|"output unwinds back up, masked first"| mask

    appr -.->|"denied, blocked, or over budget"| deny["deny_output<br/>returned to the model"]
    policies -.-> deny
    content -.-> deny
    limits -.-> deny

    class mask focal
    class deny risk
    class exec primary
    class spill,appr,judges,guard,limits,content,command,policies primary

    classDef focal    fill:none,stroke:#2F81F7,stroke-width:3px
    classDef primary  fill:none,stroke:#6e7781,stroke-width:1px
    classDef risk     fill:none,stroke:#D55E00,stroke-width:2px
    style stack fill:none,stroke:#7d8590,stroke-width:1px
